- ==========================================
- Top-Level SRAM Read Path Testbench (PTM)
- ==========================================

- Include PTM Physics-Based Model File
.include "C:/sramsa/models/ptm/ptm130.pm"

- Include Subcircuit Netlist Definitions from the netlists folder
.include "C:/sramsa/netlists/sram_cell.spice"

- Global Power Supplies
V_DD vdd 0 1.8
V_SS vss 0 0

- Module Instantiations
Xcell  q_node qb_node bl blb wl vdd vss sram_6t
Xpre   bl blb vdd pre_b sram_precharge
Xsense bl blb vdd vss saen iso out_p out_n voltage_sense_amp

- Testbench Control Clocks & Stimulus Pulses (Optimized Margins)
- Pre-charge de-asserts at 4.0ns
V_PRE  pre_b 0 pulse(1.8 0 4.0ns 0.1ns 0.1ns 10ns 20ns)

- 2. Wordline (WL) turns on at 5.0ns
V_WL   wl    0 pulse(0 1.8 5.0ns 0.1ns 0.1ns 10ns 20ns)

- 3. Isolation (ISO) turns on at 5.2ns (allowing bitlines to develop differential swing)
V_ISO  iso   0 pulse(0 1.8 5.2ns 0.1ns 0.1ns 10ns 20ns)

- 4. Sense Enable (SAEN) fires at 6.0ns (after differential voltage is established)
V_SAEN saen  0 pulse(0 1.8 6.0ns 0.1ns 0.1ns 10ns 20ns)

- Simulation Control & Automated Measurements
.control
  * Force initial voltage states
  ic v(out_p)=1.8 v(out_n)=1.8 v(q_node)=0 v(qb_node)=1.8 v(bl)=1.8 v(blb)=1.8

  op
  tran 0.01ns 15ns

  * --- Clean Automated Timing Measurements (Aligned to 0.9V Threshold) ---
  meas tran t_wl_rise WHEN v(wl)=0.9 rise=1 from=4ns to=8ns
  meas tran t_out_fall WHEN v(out_p)=0.9 fall=1 from=5ns to=10ns

  * Calculate true positive Read Access Time (t_AA)
  let t_aa = t_out_fall - t_wl_rise
  print t_aa

  write C:/sramsa/results/sram_tran.raw v(bl) v(blb) v(out_p) v(out_n) v(wl) v(saen)
.endc

.end